    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d349">

                <pb facs="0513" n="497" sameAs="frus:frus1948v09/pg497"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.00/3–1648: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Embassy in Guatemala
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-03-19T19:00:00-05:00">March 19, 1948—7
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>116. Deep concern is felt by Dept over reports indicating official Guatemalan
                    arms and ammunition being used in Costa Rica (San José telegram to Dept, No 98,
                    March 18<anchor n="1" xml:id="d349-f1"/>). You are requested to seek early
                    interview with President Arévalo in order to refer to these reports and obtain
                    statement Guatemalan position. In this connection Dept refers again to Depcirtel Jan 17.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thorp</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
